WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:05.090
Doctor Strange is a master class in visual
effects and taps into a whole new dimension—several

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.560
of them, actually—for the Marvel Cinematic
Universe to explore.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.540
But with so many elements in play, from time
manipulation to the multiverse to metaphysics

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.570
and even magic flying cloaks, there was so
much to explain that there were bound to be

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.539
a few loose ends left straggling.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:22.660
Here are some of the major questions Doctor
Strange left unanswered.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.289
"You're a man looking at the world through
a keyhole."

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:30.159
Fair warning: This video is filled with spoilers,
so those who haven't seen the movie yet should

00:00:30.159 --> 00:00:32.550
hang out in another dimension for the time
being.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.730
Why Earth?

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.431
As with many of Marvel's movie properties,
our mega-villain of the day, Dormammu, is

00:00:37.431 --> 00:00:39.850
a creature that defies all logic.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:45.780
He — or should we say it — is a being
existing outside time and space that likes

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.820
to feed on the many "generous" parts of the
universe that give life... and he's set a

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.110
giant purple eye on Earth.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:56.950
Of all planets, why does our blue-green blob
become such an important conquest for Dormammu?

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.080
Our best guess is it wouldn't be a movie if
not — that's why.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.490
How Ancient?

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:06.281
Doctor Strange asks the question we're all
wondering about—exactly how ancient is the

00:01:06.281 --> 00:01:07.281
Ancient One?

00:01:07.281 --> 00:01:08.799
We never find out.

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:13.619
Mordo does spill some vague details about
how she's of Celtic descent but nobody knows

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:14.770
anything more than that.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:19.950
We can only imagine how she became this bald,
scarred, sophisticated wizard, and certainly

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.810
have no idea why she'd stick around Earth
if she had unlimited access to the entire

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.899
continuum of existence.

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:27.540
Why Mordo?

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.939
Mordo came to the Ancient One with an injury
of his own, but we don't know any details.

00:01:30.939 --> 00:01:34.749
More importantly, it isn't clear why he was
ever chosen to be the Ancient One's apparent

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:35.990
second in command.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.520
She certainly doesn't inspire confidence when
she tells Strange that she thinks Mordo has

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.590
an inflexible soul and can only conjure up
"he's strong" as a compliment for the character.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:49.319
Why did she pluck him to be her right-hand
man if she thought he was so stiff?

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:50.450
Palmer who?

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:54.520
Obviously, Doctor Strange and Christine Palmer
have a history together, but we aren't getting

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:55.670
the whole story here.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.840
On the one hand, he's quick to lash out at
her cruel words that demean their past romance.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.469
On the other, he clings to a watch she gave
him with an inscription about their love standing

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:10.649
the test of time and turns to her multiple
times for help, so what gives?

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:12.150
What's the magic rule?

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.740
Those sorcerer protégés were pretty loose-lipped
about Kamar-Taj, weren't they?

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:20.019
Pangborn knew Strange for all of two minutes
before he let the source of his healing slip,

00:02:20.019 --> 00:02:23.709
and Mordo was quick to guide him there, no
questions asked, when he heard him mutter

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.159
the name in passing.

00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:28.659
It's all a matter of moving the plot along
in both cases, of course, but are there any

00:02:28.659 --> 00:02:32.980
rules to when, how, or why you can just divulge
this information to strangers?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.440
Seems like they might be a little more guarded
about their precious sanctuary is all we're

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:36.940
sayin'.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:37.540
"Teach me"

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:39.900
Whose cloak?

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.540
We're told the Cloak of Levitation is a fickle
creature, but that's basically all we know

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:44.540
about it.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.959
It's a compliment to Strange that the Cloak
has chosen him, but why?

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:49.319
What became of its last owner?

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:51.299
Did the Ancient One know this person?

00:02:51.299 --> 00:02:52.390
Is it a sentient being?

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:56.290
The other magical artifacts we saw didn't
seem to have such strong personalities, so

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.819
what makes the Cloak so different?

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:01.140
No hands?

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:05.659
When Strange first joins the crew at Kamar-Taj,
he's not strong enough to heal his damaged

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:10.150
hands, but after he ascends to untold strength
and capability, he's still not able — or

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:13.909
perhaps not willing? — to undo the nerve
damage to his hands.

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:17.750
Is it because the one-handed master showed
off his fire-spinning skills and changed his

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:18.750
mind?

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.530
Or is he just incapable of willing his cells
and nerves to correct themselves?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.969
Hard to say.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:23.969
No mask?

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:28.769
Kaecilius and his cohorts all got some purple
skin masks, complete with scaly Stone Man

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:31.489
rot around their eyes, once they started channeling
dark power.

00:03:31.489 --> 00:03:36.310
However, they only shared one facial tell
with the Ancient One, who'd done the same:

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.680
The insignia on their foreheads.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.569
Why is it that she was immune to the Dormammu
mask, but not the symbol, when she was channeling

00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:44.480
dark power?

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.480
Why wait?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.349
It doesn't really make sense for the Ancient
One to die when she does.

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:52.019
Remember her big speech about how the body
has the ability to heal itself with the right

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:53.140
spiritual motivation?

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:56.931
No matter how grave her wounds might have
been during the battle with Kaecilius, she

00:03:56.931 --> 00:03:59.150
should've been able to help herself.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:06.620
Unless this was kind of an Obi-Wan Kenobi,
help Luke with the Force kinda thing…

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.370
But then, we've still got some other questions.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:12.010
Doctor Strange definitely had the ability
to manipulate time by the point of her ultimate

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.670
injury, so why didn't he whip out his event
reversal trick to save her … or the London

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.410
Sanctum … or undo everything in New York,
for that matter?

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.470
"This doesn't make any sense."

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:23.480
"Not everything has to"

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:24.480
Okay.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.150
No fair?

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.591
When Doctor Strange banishes Kaecilius and
his lackeys to Dormammu's dimension, they

00:04:29.591 --> 00:04:33.250
float up and are instantly flayed alive—or
so it seems.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.870
He says they're still getting their wish for
eternal life, but it isn't going to be pleasant.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.650
What Strange experienced during his limited
time in Dormammu's dimension was an endless

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.389
barrage of brutality.

00:04:42.389 --> 00:04:45.050
Are we to assume that's what's coming their
way, too?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.770
They're obviously in the doghouse after picking
the fight that led Doctor Strange to Dormammu's

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:53.650
breakfast nook, but Kaecilius was clearly
a powerful sorcerer, so Dormammu will probably

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.590
keep him on his team, right?

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:56.680
Why Pangborn?

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:01.090
In the post-credits scene, Mordo has broken
bad after learning that the Ancient One had

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:04.139
been lying to him and drawing on dark energy.

00:05:04.139 --> 00:05:08.710
Mordo's new mission is to trim down the list
of magicians around the world, and his first

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:12.180
victim of sorcery-stripping is Jonathan Pangborn.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:17.090
This was a guy who had nothing to do with
any of this stuff and expressly chose not

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.699
to be a part of the Ancient One's army.

00:05:18.699 --> 00:05:19.750
So why him?

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:23.740
Was Mordo getting vengeance for Pangborn sending
Strange to Kamar-Taj, or was the guy just

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.300
doing more than shooting hoops in his downtime?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.530
Thanks for watching!

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:29.730
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel and watch more videos like

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:30.919
the one you just saw.

00:05:30.919 --> 00:05:33.830
And don't forget to check out all this cool
